Three interleaved checkouts, one failure, zero attribution: every line lacks a ___b1___, so the error cannot be tied to a user, a ticket, or its own request's other lines. It must be minted (or accepted from the load balancer) in ___b2___ — the first hop — and forwarded on the request headers, because middleware may run in a separate edge isolate, so ___b3___ context cannot span the gap into the Node render process; the header is the bridge, and child loggers bind the id within it.

